# Service worker cache versioning

This file is the most common source of broken deploys in this repo. The
failure is always the same shape: a second stamp gets appended instead of
the existing one being replaced, and agents keep getting the old file.

Read the whole file before editing it.

1. CACHE_NAME ends in an integer. Increment it by exactly 1. Replace the
   value in place. Do not introduce a second constant.
2. For every file this PR changes, find its EXISTING entry in
   URLS_TO_CACHE and replace the ?v= value on that line.
3. A URL containing "?v=" more than once is a defect. Never append.
4. Never add a new URLS_TO_CACHE line for a path that is already listed.
   Edit the existing line.
5. The same ?v= values appear in index.html. Both files must agree.
   Update both.

## Mandatory verification before declaring done

Search both sw2.js and index.html for:

- any URL containing more than one "?v="
- any path listed twice

Report the result of that search explicitly in your summary. "I updated
the cache" without this check is not a completed task.
